    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 51 tests pass with a clean build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `readOnly` `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` default method that splits off the country code (longest recognized prefix among `{\"61\", \"1\"}` \u2014 mirroring the country codes the create endpoint uses when normalizing to E.164 \u2014 with a leading-digit fallback), then emits `+<countryCode>`, a space, and the national digits grouped in threes. E.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Non-E.164/`null` values are returned unchanged.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched and still returns E.164 (`+61412345678`), exactly as the `Cp37Tests` assertion requires.",
